{
 "file": "Emuqu/Sources/Models/UserSettings+Model.swift",
 "hash": "b8350cdc021d266c",
 "role": "Declares the UserSettings value type: every stored preference with in-memory defaults, derived values (effective max HR/LTHR/resting HR/weight/FTP, sleep schedule, merge gap, comeback/break/overreach state, population RMSSD), CodingKeys, the PerformanceFlagKey UserDefaults mirror, HealthProfileField and the iCloud-backup strip/restore helpers.",
 "types": [
  "UserSettings: struct — Codable/Equatable settings document",
  "UserSettings.DailyReportDelivery: enum — smart/fixed",
  "UserSettings.DailyReportFormat: enum — full/teaser/auto",
  "UserSettings.PerformanceFlagKey: enum — UserDefaults mirror key names",
  "UserSettings.CodingKeys: enum — JSON keys (incl. legacy smartProviderRoutingEnabled)",
  "UserSettings.BiologicalSex: enum — Male/Female/Other",
  "HealthProfileField: enum — birthday/biologicalSex/bodyWeight markers",
  "UserSettings: extension — withoutHealthFilledProfile / keepingHealthFilledProfile"
 ],
 "state": [
  "ud:perf.enableAIAssistant (key declared; read by performanceFlag, written by SettingsManager.save)",
  "ud:perf.enableVoiceMode",
  "ud:perf.enableWatchConnectivity",
  "UserSettings.currentSchemaVersion = 1 (static)"
 ],
 "toplevel": "Stored-property initializers set the in-memory defaults (sessionMergeMode .defaultGap, customMergeGapHours 4.5, sleepSplitGapMinutes 20, enablePeriodicCoachUpdates true, cadence 300, enableSleepIntegration true, peakingDetectionEnabled true, battery/sync/coach alerts true, preserveClipboard true, temperatureUnit .regionDefault, routingMode .manual, watchDisplayOnlyMode true, hasFixedTempAsymmetry true, keepScreenOn/AI/voice/watch true, defaultCaptureMode 'both', dailyReportFixedMinuteOfDay 7*60, others false/nil). Bedtime and the fixed report time are stored as wall-clock minutes after midnight (expectedBedtimeMinuteOfDay, dailyReportFixedMinuteOfDay), so a time-zone change keeps their clock time; expectedBedtime / dailyReportFixedTime are computed Date views of them. CodingKeys carries both the minute keys and the legacy Date keys.",
 "units": [
